  "title": "Vertex AI: Generation Continuation & Breaking Changes",
  "summary": "This Vertex AI v1beta1 update introduces significant breaking changes, making several properties read-only and altering a schema type. On the feature front, you can now resume long-running content generation with new continuation tokens and access detailed content metadata, including citations and grounding sources.",
  "details": "Developers should be aware of several breaking changes: the `effectiveIdentity` property in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Agent` and the `continuationToken` property in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Candidate` are now output-only and immutable. Additionally, the `customMetadata` property within `GenaiVertexV1beta1FileCitation` has changed its underlying type from a specific reference to a more generic object, which may impact strongly typed client implementations.\n\nNew capabilities include robust support for resuming long-running content generation via `continuationToken` fields added to `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1GenerateContentRequest`, `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Candidate`, `GenaiVertexV1beta1Interaction`, and `GenaiVertexV1beta1InteractionStatusUpdate`. The `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1Candidate` also gains a `CONTINUATION` finish reason. You can now retrieve rich `contentMetadata` (citations, grounding sources) alongside generated content in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1SchemaPromptSpecStructuredPrompt`. Other enhancements include `tileSmoothing` for improved video super-resolution, a `DISABLED` network egress mode for `GenaiVertexV1beta1EnvironmentConfigEgressRule`, and customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK) support for `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1AgentAnomalyDetectionScope`.",
